## Context

The article (report/report.tex line ~183) documents that 211/280 outputs
were generated with default temperature (~1.0) rather than temperature=0.
Ticket 0084 added the limitation paragraph and enforced t=0 going forward.

The slides (slides/slides.tex) present ablation and benchmark results
without noting this confound. A reviewer seeing only the slides would
not know about the t≈1 vs t=0 issue.

## Actions

1. Add a bullet or footnote in slides/slides.tex near the results
   slides noting the temperature limitation for pre-PR#244 runs.

## Test

`make slides` compiles. Temperature caveat is present.

## Exit criteria

- slides/slides.tex mentions temperature limitation
- LaTeX builds without errors
